    <exercise number="5" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Describe how to graph $$y = \left| {x - 3} \right|$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>We start by finding the x-intercept, or where the function = 0. Once we have that point, which is $$(3,0), (3,0),$$ we graph to the right the straight line graph $$y=x-3, y=x-3,$$ and then when we draw it to the left we plot positive y values, taking the absolute value of them.</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
