    <heading level="1">Real-World Applications</heading>
    <exercise number="63" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>In chemistry the volume for a certain gas is given by $$V = 20T,$$ where V is measured in cc and T is temperature in ºC. If the temperature varies between 80ºC and 120ºC, find the set of volume values.</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$80\le T\le 120 1,600\le 20T\le 2,400 80\le T\le 120 1,600\le 20T\le 2,400$$</paragraph>
        <paragraph>$$[ 1,600, 2,400 ] [ 1,600, 2,400 ]$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
